# SmartSumbong — project-root web-server rules.
#
# Written ahead of real hosting (6 Sep 2026), not for the local `php -S`
# dev server (which ignores .htaccess entirely — this only matters once
# a real Apache host points its document root at this project folder,
# the same layout config.php and transparency.php's own relative paths
# already assume; see that discussion for why).
#
# Apache-specific and UNTESTED against a real host, since none is picked
# yet. Verify this actually works (and adjust the syntax if the eventual
# host runs something other than Apache 2.4+, or has mod_rewrite/
# mod_headers disabled) before relying on it in production.
#
# What this defends against: once the document root is this folder, the
# .env file sitting right here (real Supabase keys) would otherwise be
# directly downloadable at https://yourdomain/.env, and things like
# supabase/, mobile/, and this README have no business being served over
# HTTP at all. Only admin/ (behind its own login) and public/ (the
# transparency page) are meant to answer a request.

# Block every dotfile outright — .env, .git, .env.example, etc.
<FilesMatch "^\.">
    Require all denied
</FilesMatch>

# Block everything except the two folders this project actually serves.
# (The bare root "/" is intentionally not aliased to public/transparency.php
# here — decide that once a real domain exists and it's clear whether the
# barangay wants the public page to BE the homepage.)
RewriteEngine On
RewriteCond %{REQUEST_URI} !^/admin/
RewriteCond %{REQUEST_URI} !^/public/
RewriteRule ^ - [F]
